1. Definitions

"Licensor" means the copyright holder identified above.

"Software" means the VisionGuard source code, object code, documentation, and
other materials distributed with this license, excluding Third-Party
Components.

"Official Visual Client" means a VisionGuard client designated by the Licensor
as part of the free pure-software visual edition. At the publication date of
this license, these are the WinForms, WPF, and Android visual detector clients.

"Pure Software Visual Use" means running an Official Visual Client on a
general-purpose personal computer, workstation, phone, or tablet to perform
screen, window, or camera-based visual detection, together with the VisionGuard
Server and Receiver functions necessary for that software-only alert workflow.
A built-in camera, a general-purpose USB camera, or screen capture used directly
by an Official Visual Client does not by itself constitute Hardware Detector
Use.

"Hardware Detector" means a dedicated physical detector, sensor, embedded
computer, edge computer, gateway, appliance, or detection unit that connects
to, is controlled or managed by, or sends observations, status, or events to
the Software. Examples include an Edge Detector, PIR sensor, millimeter-wave
sensor, door contact, vibration sensor, environmental sensor, dedicated camera
appliance, industrial controller, or sensor gateway.

"Hardware Detector Use" means developing, testing, activating, connecting,
controlling, managing, operating, or providing support for one or more Hardware
Detectors through the Software. It does not include Pure Software Visual Use.

"Internal Use" means use by you and your personnel solely for your own personal
or organizational operations. Internal Use does not include making the
Software or its functionality available to third parties as a product, hosted
service, managed service, bureau service, or other external service.

"Third-Party Components" means software, models, libraries, assets, or other
materials identified as being provided by third parties or distributed under a
separate license.

